    "reading": {
        "body": "Two AI provider security incidents were open as of September 2, 2026, out of twelve tracked providers, down from a peak of four open incidents on August 21 and 24.\n\nLambda accounts for the largest share of incident observations by a wide margin: 62 of its 107 tracked observations coincided with an incident, against 18 of 113 for OpenAI and single digits for the rest of the field. That concentration lines up with Lambda's uptime figures elsewhere in this site's data, where it also reported the lowest healthy rate of any tracked provider, at 42.1 percent, suggesting its uptime and incident problems are the same underlying pattern counted two ways rather than two separate issues.\n\nThe daily open-incident count fell steadily across the second half of August, from 4 on August 21 to 0 on both August 30 and 31, before rising again to 2 by September 2, so the improvement was not permanent. This data counts incident observations and open counts, not root causes, severity, or resolution times, so it supports identifying which providers see AI security incidents most often, not what those incidents were.",
